   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Age",
     "texto": [
      "In Polish, age is expressed with **mam**, **masz** or **ma** plus the number and the right form of «year». English uses «to be» («I am twenty»); Polish uses «to have», as in «I have twenty years»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Rok, lata, lat",
     "texto": [
      "You say **jeden rok** (one year), **dwa/trzy/cztery lata** (two, three or four years) and **pięć lat** (five years).",
      "In this lesson we practise these common forms; the endings do not always work the same as in English."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Forms of the verb mieć",
     "texto": [
      "**Mam** = I have, **masz** = you have, **ma** = he/she has. The subject can be left out if it is already clear."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
